      {
        "title": "",
        "id": "",
        "text": {
          "content": "# hapi-fhir — JVM / Tomcat / DB pool internals\n\nFour process-level metrics scraped directly from HAPI FHIR's own `/actuator/prometheus` endpoint, distinct from the container/node-level view in the unified **Arogyam Platform** dashboard. **No tile here filters by cluster**, so despite the \"(staging)\" name, every chart mixes **aa-stg and aa-prod** pods on the same lines — open a series' details or check its resource labels if you need to isolate one environment.\n\nThis dashboard's unique value is the two panels the unified dashboard doesn't have: **DB connections**, which is the HikariCP pool HAPI uses to talk to Cloud SQL (exhausting this pool looks like slow/hanging requests upstream, well before Cloud SQL itself shows any strain), and **Active Tomcat sessions**. **Watch for:** the pending-connections line rising above 0 for any length of time (the pool is maxed out and requests are queuing), or JVM memory climbing without recovering after a collection.",
          "format": "MARKDOWN",
          "style": {
            "backgroundColor": "",
            "horizontalAlignment": "H_LEFT",
            "padding": "P_EXTRA_SMALL",
            "pointerLocation": "POINTER_LOCATION_UNSPECIFIED",
            "textColor": "",
            "verticalAlignment": "V_TOP"
          }
        }
      },
      {
